WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.052 --> 00:00:02.970
- [Narrator] Where can
you see the Eiffel Tower,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.776
Mont Saint Michel, and the Arc De Triomphe

00:00:05.776 --> 00:00:07.876
all within a few steps of each other?

00:00:07.876 --> 00:00:09.359
France, of course.

00:00:09.359 --> 00:00:11.276
Well, Miniature France.

00:00:16.546 --> 00:00:19.092
Located two hours outside of Paris,

00:00:19.092 --> 00:00:20.780
Miniature France is a theme park

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.559
made in the image of real France,

00:00:22.559 --> 00:00:26.226
but at 1/30 of the original size.

00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:29.310
The park is 12 acres in size

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.666
and features 117 different monuments.

00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:33.945
Miniature France was built by

00:00:33.945 --> 00:00:37.136
a team of 50 model makers
and landscape architects,

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:39.960
ensuring that each model
is an exact replica

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.127
of its larger counterpart.

00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:45.919
To make this hybrid city come to life,

00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:48.115
there are animated
trains, cars, and planes

00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:50.448
that move around the region.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.574
And while you might not have time to see

00:00:53.574 --> 00:00:56.527
all the real France has
to offer in one day,

00:00:56.527 --> 00:00:59.970
you can make your way around
this park in one afternoon,

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.553
although your photos
might not be to scale.

